The attached image, Figure 4 from the 2015 paper, illustrates the enhanced uptake of antigen (OVA) by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs) when formulated with Nano-11. Confocal microscopy reveals that while soluble FITC-labeled ovalbumin (green) alone shows minimal internalization, AF647-labeled Nano-11 (red) is efficiently phagocytized by BMDCs. When OVA is adsorbed to Nano-11, both are strongly co-localized within the cells, indicating that Nano-11 significantly boosts the intracellular delivery of antigen to dendritic cells, a critical mechanism for stimulating an effective immune response, as discussed in the paper's findings.